    "category": "security",
    "evidence": "Probes in /tmp/uri_review_R37/p2.py and p3.py: has_link_or_contact False for 'refunds-portal ~ \u04410\u043c' (Cyrillic \u0441, digit 0, Cyrillic \u043c), 'refunds-portal . \u04410\u043c', 'refunds-portal [.] \u04410\u043c', 'refunds-portal \u04410\u043c' (core domain, plain space), 'refunds-portal ~ \u04cf0\u04cf', 'refunds-portal . \u04cf0\u04cf' (.lol), 'refunds-portal ~ |\u043e\u0406' (.lol), 'refunds-portal ~ \u0455|' (.sl). In SENT 'Claim your energy rebate refund at {} before the deadline.': verify() keeps the claim with [1], extractive() keeps the sentence, surface.clean returns it unmasked, and validate._no_urls reports no error. Detected for comparison: 'refunds-portal ~ \u04410m', '~ c0\u043c', '~ \u0441\u043e\u043c'. Cause: _RUN=[A-Za-z0-9|]+ isolates the lone '0'/'|' among non-ASCII letters (letters<2, no TLD reading), and the skeleton/Unicode fold does not map 0/1/I/|. All of these characters are listed in the UTS #39 data, so D29 does not cover them. Also, mask_links('Go to refunds-portal \u04410\u043c/claim now') gives 'Go to refunds-portal [X] now', which leaves the name on screen, while '\u0441\u043e\u043c/claim' and 'c0m/claim' are fully masked.",
    "files": [
     "uri_web/untrusted.py:790",
     "uri_web/untrusted.py:808",
     "uri_web/untrusted.py:829",
     "uri_web/untrusted.py:837",
     "uri_web/untrusted.py:846",
     "uri_web/surface.py:38",
     "uri_a2ui/validate.py:150"
    ],
    "id": "R37-01",
    "owner_decision": false,
    "severity": "HIGH",
    "suggested_fix": "Apply the ASCII look-alike fold to the skeleton text as well (or fold 0/1/I/| inside the skeleton map), so endings are read with both fold sets at once. Add regressions for the mixed forms and for full masking of the name.",
    "title": "R1-01/R31-01 class still open: an ending mixing confusables-listed Cyrillic look-alikes with an ASCII look-alike ('\u04410\u043c', '\u04cf0\u04cf', '|\u043e\u0406', '\u0455|') is folded by neither the skeleton nor _ascii_variant, so it passes has_link_or_contact, verify(), extractive(), the research surface and the A2UI validator (W1-AC12/AC15, D16/D29)"
   }
